{#- The front page's box (targum-internal#399), drawn wherever a stranger may try a link:
    the front door, and since targum-internal#676 /after-duolingo-hebrew.

    Paste a link and be told what it is, in the Add box's own sentence. A plain post, so
    it works with JavaScript off; the answer comes back on the page the box stands on.
    Nothing is built and nothing is spent (`Library.describe`), and no percentage is
    shown: "you know X%" needs a record, and getting one is the reason to join
    (2026-09-30).

    `try_on` names the page the box stands on when it is not the front door. It rides in
    the form as `on`, so `/try` answers on that page, and the waitlist's form under an
    answer says it was pressed there (`joined_from`). Empty is the front door.

    `joined_from`, where it is not the front door's `/`, rides in the form as `from`, so
    the tag a link to the page carried (`serve.came_from`) survives a try. -#}
<div class="try" id="try">
  <form class="try-form" method="post" action="/try{% if asked %}?lang={{ asked }}{% endif %}#try">
    {%- if try_on|default('') %}
    <input type="hidden" name="on" value="{{ try_on }}">
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if joined_from|default('/') != "/" %}
    {#- The tag the page was opened with, carried through a try (#676). #}
    <input type="hidden" name="from" value="{{ joined_from }}">
    {%- endif %}
    <label class="field">
      <input type="url" name="link" required inputmode="url" autocapitalize="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="{{ t("landing.try.placeholder", "Paste a link to anything in Hebrew") }}" aria-label="{{ t("landing.try.label", "A link to try") }}"{% if tried and tried.link %} value="{{ tried.link }}"{% endif %}>
      <button class="btn tonal" type="submit">{{ t("landing.try.button", "Try it") }}</button>
    </label>
  </form>
  {%- if tried %}
  <div class="tried" role="status">
    {%- if tried.refused %}
    <p class="tried-what">{{ tried.refused }}</p>
    {%- else %}
    {#- The thing they pasted leads (David, 2026-10-02: the answer read as a form
        letter): a mark for its kind, drawn like the tiles in "Your own Hebrew", its
        title in the reading face, then the one sentence the Add box would say. -#}
    {%- set kind = 'video' if tried.door in ('youtube', 'instagram', 'tiktok', 'facebook') else ('post' if tried.door in ('x', 'instagram-post') else ('podcast' if tried.door == 'podcast' else 'page')) %}
    <div class="tried-card">
      <span class="tried-mark" aria-hidden="true">
        {%- if kind == 'video' %}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M9 7.5v9l7.5-4.5z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
        {%- elif kind == 'post' %}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="7" cy="8" r="2.2" fill="currentColor"/><rect x="11" y="6.8" width="7.5" height="2.2" rx="1.1" fill="currentColor"/><rect x="5" y="12.6" width="13.5" height="2.2" rx="1.1" fill="currentColor"/><rect x="5" y="16.6" width="9" height="2.2" rx="1.1" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
        {%- elif kind == 'podcast' %}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><g fill="currentColor"><rect x="4" y="10" width="2" height="4" rx="1"/><rect x="8" y="7" width="2" height="10" rx="1"/><rect x="12" y="4.5" width="2" height="15" rx="1"/><rect x="16" y="8" width="2" height="8" rx="1"/><rect x="20" y="10.5" width="2" height="3" rx="1"/></g></svg>
        {%- else %}<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="5.5" y="3.5" width="13" height="17" rx="2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><g fill="currentColor"><rect x="8.5" y="7.5" width="7" height="1.6" rx="0.8"/><rect x="8.5" y="11" width="7" height="1.6" rx="0.8"/><rect x="8.5" y="14.5" width="4.5" height="1.6" rx="0.8"/></g></svg>{% endif -%}
      </span>
      <div class="tried-body">
        {%- if tried.title %}
        <p class="tried-title" dir="auto">{{ tried.title }}</p>
        {%- endif %}
        <p class="tried-what">
          {%- if tried.door == 'youtube' %}{{ t("landing.try.youtube", "That’s a YouTube video") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'instagram' %}{{ t("landing.try.instagram", "That’s an Instagram reel") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'instagram-post' %}{{ t("landing.try.instagram-post", "That’s an Instagram post") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'tiktok' %}{{ t("landing.try.tiktok", "That’s a TikTok video") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'facebook' %}{{ t("landing.try.facebook", "That’s a Facebook video") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'x' %}{{ t("landing.try.x", "That’s a post on X") }}
          {%- elif tried.door == 'podcast' %}{{ t("landing.try.podcast", "That’s a podcast episode") }}
          {%- else %}{{ t("landing.try.page", "That’s a page from {site}", site=tried.site) }}{% endif %}
          {%- if tried.minutes %}, {{ tn("landing.try.minutes", tried.minutes, "{n} minute", "{n} minutes") }}{% endif %}
          {%- if tried.sentences %}, {{ tn("landing.try.sentences", tried.sentences, "{n} sentence", "{n} sentences") }}{% endif %}
          {%- if tried.subtitles %}, {{ t("landing.try.subtitles", "Hebrew subtitles written by a person") }}{% endif %}.</p>
        {#- No wait here (beta review PUB-02, 2026-11-03): the address joins a waitlist,
            and the build comes when the operator lets them in, which may be weeks.
            "Ready in about 4 minutes" promised what the door cannot keep (§6).
            With the door open (design.md §12, 2026-11-10) the link waits for them
            in Upload instead, got ready on their own press: nothing is built here. -#}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="tried-keep">{% if door_is_open() %}{{ t("open-door.link-waiting-for-you", "Sign up and this link will be waiting for you.") }}{% else %}{{ t("landing.try.turned-into-a-lesson", "Join the waitlist and we’ll have this ready for you when your turn comes.") }}{% endif %}</p>
    {% with note = false, link = tried.link %}{% include '_join_form.html.j2' %}{% endwith %}
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
  {%- endif %}
</div>
